Key Differences at a Glance
Feature	AWS Fargate	Amazon EC2
Infrastructure Management	Serverless (AWS manages all patching, scaling, and provisioning).	Full Control (You manage OS patches, instance scaling, and security hardening).

Feature	Security Group	Network ACL (NACL)
Level	Instance level (ENI / EC2)	Subnet level
State	Stateful (tracks connection state)	Stateless (no memory of connections)
Rules	Only Allow rules	Both Allow & Deny rules
Rule Evaluation	All rules evaluated together	Rules evaluated in number order (lowest first)
Return Traffic	Automatically allowed	Must be explicitly allowed
Default Behavior	Deny all inbound, allow all outbound	Allow all inbound & outbound (default NACL)
Association	Can be attached to multiple instances	Attached to subnets
Rule Types	Simpler	More granular (CIDR + rule numbers)

